                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Men of Valor- The horrors of Vietnam for all the wrong reasons.\r\n\r\nLet me preface by saying I've been playing shooters for twenty plus years. I have 5,000 plus hours on RO: Darkest Hour and served in the military myself.  Not trying to toot my own horn but I have a good idea of what I'm doing.\r\n\r\nMen of Valor doesn't give a damn. It's going to take a huge jank dump on your head. I had to play this game on easy and cheat for several portions of the game just to finish it. You can get taken out quickly in an unguarded moment, which is fine. Any shooter I'm always moving cover to cover, checking corners, etc....but this games jank shines in that enemies will shoot through walls, snipe you across the map through dense foliage, somehow shoot you while prone behind cover (wtf?), your friends are blind and often in the way, and enemies spawn from literally anywhere around you nonstop until you reach a point to trigger the next segment. While you can search enemies for ammo, weapons, aid supplies - this is an awkward time consuming step where you can be ambushed at any moment.  \r\n\r\nI get what they were going for and it did instill a fear and paranoia in me while patrolling through the dense jungles and swamps. The game does have some neat sections (the tunnels and portions of Hue were cool), but these are pretty rare. More often than not, you'll slog through dense ass bush, dodging non-stop NVA and booby traps, to get to a bunker sections where you have to bound up to a point of cover to throw smoke for an airstrike... not like the RTO could just call in the coordinates himself, need to send out the black dude. I don't really care about any of the characters either and the story is cliche.  There are points that are ludicrous, as well. The opening mission, the Marines take indirect fire and the LT decides to have the men form up during this to give them orders....maybe they should run for cover? Or I loved the dudes sitting in their underwear wearing sunglasses (at night) smoking weed while their base was being shelled and overrun (give me a break). \r\n\r\nOverall, not a fun experience.",
